WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
Good morning, John. I'm here today with

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.000
Michael Aranda.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.120
Mike: Hello!

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.000
Hank: Introduce yourself.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.000
M: My name is Michael Aranda.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.660
H: I framed this shot poorly.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.920
Today, Michael and I are going to be putting together the Millennium Falcon.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.060
(musical fanfare)

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.560
Why are they making you do the people first?

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.200
The people seem like they're the most fun part.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.480
You should save that for last.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.460
I think this is Han's hair.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.960
Somebody's legs.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.160
Where are all the heads‽

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.000
Han Solo is complete!

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.080
The thing was not cheap by the way.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.260
It took me a couple guesses

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:34.940
...to guess how much it cost.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.800
They forgot to number this bag!

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.520
Thank goodness that he figured that out 'cause I would never have.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.280
What the frick.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:42.360
*Beeping sound.*

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.460
I figured it was going to make a noise.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:44.400
What did you think of that, Lemon?

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.320
Don't like it! She doesn't like it!

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.900
We're on to pack 2!

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.020
(Evil laugh)

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:59.380
(music plays)

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.540
What is this?

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.600
I don't know.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.740
All right pieces, like make Lego happen.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:05.760
What are these?

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.780
What are all these?!

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.080
This this is fro- this is still from bag two!

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.320
M: Wasn't this bag one. Oh look! We're going to use it right now!

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.330
H: We are! Where do you put it?

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.460
M: I don't know, hold it.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.540
While, you do the rest in the page 75... no tube. Where is the other book?

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.600
Hank: Dude, the tube will happen when the tube happens.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.300
(music plays)

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.000
H: They're pastel! What do they taste like?

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.720
M: Like Reese's....pieces, but...harder.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:37.020
H: Harder, yeah! I don't like them. I did this wrong!!!

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.280
We're installing the tube part which Michael was very excited about earlier.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:41.920
M:Tubular!

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.300
H:Really? Yeah?

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.900
Perfectum!  Last page...

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.360
of the first book.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:55.320
M:Careful. I dropped an egg in my cleavage.
(Hank laughs)

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:00.760
(music plays)

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:01.980
H: We're on to number five.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.100
Show them the Millennium Falcon as it currently exists.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:06.780
Ah, God, it's scary.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.400
We put the feet on, we've got a blaster on the bottom.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.699
H:Interior living space is done. 
M:One of the blasters came apart.

00:02:11.699 --> 00:02:12.610
H:Nooooo! Sh-

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.550
It's like every time you finish a bag, it like

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:17.580
... is from harder to easier to easier to easier to find pieces,

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.680
then you start a new bag and it's like, ARGHHH!

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.780
It's hard again! Cardigan! Madmartigan!! Tartigrade!

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:24.800
It's late.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.480
So now going to continue our build.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:33.120
(music plays)

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:37.620
It is now 2 o'clock in the morning. Michael is finished with his Mountain Dew.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.640
The Millenium Falcon has another, uh, blaster on it.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.000
It actually looks pretty much like the Millennium Falcon right now.  Bag number 6!

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:48.780
Careful! Couldn't do it, people!

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.920
Awww!

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.700
I don't know what's happening. Awwww!

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.700
(laughter)

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.320
(music plays)

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.260
Everyone, it's finished.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.240
(Hank makes spaceship noises)

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:28.040
(music plays)

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:30.820
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

